	"_note": "THE SLOPED PLATE, the primitive that replaced the room. Rooms were deleted because an axis-aligned box that expands to four walls, a floor and a ceiling can only draw a shed. Everything above the deck here is ONE primitive - a quad with four independent 3D corners and a thickness - differing only in numbers: a lower tier tapered in plan and tumbled home with a front that overhangs 0.45 m; a wheelhouse SET BACK on all four sides with a 0.85 m forward-raked windscreen, a reverse-raked aft bulkhead and a roof sloping 0.25 m down aft; a funnel of four tapering plates raked aft under a black cap; a bulwark knuckle flaring 0.30 m outboard; and a raked transom. 18 plates, 24 openings, no boxes. The bulwarks and cap rails below are the existing wall/deck primitives, unchanged, so the deckhouse is the only thing under test. Bow is -Z, so plan z=0 is the stem and the 45 degree taper occupies z=0..5.",
